<title>USA: ADR REPORT - Cott Corp rises.</title>
<headline>ADR REPORT - Cott Corp rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian beverage company Cott Corp rose in heavy volume Friday to highlight trade in American Depositary Receipts  ADRs and foreign shares.</p>
<p>Cott rose 11/16 to 11-1/4 after it reported first-quarter earnings per share increased to C$0.17 from C$0.12 for the same period a year before.</p>
<p>Volume in mid-afternoon was 1.7 million shares, putting the company among the most active foreign shares and ADRs.  </p>
<p>Among other active ADRs, Britain's Vodafone Group Plc rose 3/4 to 48-3/4, a 12-month high, and Brazilian phone company Telebras SA was up 3/8 to 141-5/8.</p>
<p>Mexico's Vitro SA rose 3/4 to 10-1/8.</p>
<p>((-- Wall Street desk (212) 859-1730))</p>
</text>
